ddie gray or the  Cambridge police acted stupidly black  lives matter in all these groups what do  we want dead cops  we want them now I sometimes worry and  wonder that the this younger generation  may not have a full and complete  understanding of how dangerous police  work is a my hope I'm wrong on that but  one of that yeah I mean look I think  everybody knows police work is dangerous  and I think at the same time everybody  knows that sometimes police cross the  line it just does happen Sean in any  profession people cross the line a  percentage everybody at tiny come shop  and I understand that but what I'm  saying is I think that if anything is  happening now I think people are just at  some point they're just saying stop this  violence you know it's like you one side  can blame another side another side can  blend that side but the fact is the  violence keeps happening and at a point  what's you know what good is it to say  oh you didn't know you did it oh no you  did it it's like at a point it's just  got to stop because this is impacting  the way we live now I mean this is do  you go to an outdoor concert do you go  to a movie theater do you send your kid  through school what about flying I mean  at a point if you look at it this  everything is closing in on us and to me  it's not about blame it's this this has  got to stop this is got Justin oh I  totally agree I love the fact that  there's kind of two sides of you you  know there's the funny outrageous crazy  Harvey that I've known for years and you  you or have a really serious side and  your new shows been a big hit on the  channel and you did Simon Cowell and  Judge Judy and this weekend you're doing  a really good a big friend of mine  Prime Minister Netanyahu I want to run a  quick clip and it runs Sunday night at  8:00 I went to an American high school  in the 60s right can you imagine you  went to Chilton Hamm high school yeah so  be honest with me who's the most famous  alum you are Reggie Jackson in Israel me  in America Reggie Jackson by you know a  hundred yards oh my gosh you know I love  well first of all I know him personally  I love that you get these another side  of people you're asking questions that  they don't get asked in normal  interviews and and look the idea here is  to me it's almost a psychological hour  that I want to know how these enormous  ly successful people accomplished people  became who they are today with lessons  they learned along the way and you know  with with the prime minister  you know he I'm sure you know the Shan  but we really got into it he he has a  disdain for politics and aggressively  does not want his children to be  political or to be to run for office he  has he finds it suffocating and he finds  it cruel and you know he talks to me  about this and I knew about how much his  brother's death impacted him but to sit  there and talk to him about it and  really kind of get into it and watch him  cry was really moving to me that that's  the raid on Entebbe  alright objective file the I promise  I'll be watching I won't miss us it's  hosted by Harvey Levin Sunday night 8:00  p.m. Eastern right here on Fox

